> advantages to using a mount as a samurai? Has this ever worked out for
> anyone?
>
> Thanks-

A warhorse has speed 24, which is significantly better than a player
with speed boots. Add a zap of speed monster, and its speed (and yours,
if riding) is better than anything but an air elemental's. Kicking the
steed will make it gallop, giving additional speed. This applies to
movement only, not player actions taken while riding - but you'll still
be able to escape from almost any situation with that kind of speed.

Saddles are fairly rare. I'd suggest making use of it with your
warhorse. Once you spend 2000 turns riding, you will be able to pick up
items without dismounting. The only problem is keeping horses alive.
They will eat food rations if starving, but it may be too late by the
time you realize the horse is starving. Kelp fronds (from diving on
Medusa or Juiblex) are an easy source of horsefood, if you have the
right equipment.



